<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM DEP DROPS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES THURS.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM DEP DROPS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES THURS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gasoline prices will be lowered by 2.50 drachmas per litre and diesel prices will drop by 0.20 per litre, effective on Thursday and for one week, Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after lower world gasoline prices, down by $11.2 per metric tonne and a softer dollar/drachma parity, down by 0.6 drachmas, it said. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
